                            <comment id="499615" author="gerrit" created="Fri, 14 Aug 2026 05:13:37 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&quot;Keguang Xu &amp;lt;kxu@ddn.com&amp;gt;&quot; uploaded a new patch: &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/67998&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/67998&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Subject: &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20566&quot; title=&quot;FLR-EC: recover data from parity code for DIO+AIO&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-20566&quot;&gt;LU-20566&lt;/a&gt; ec: reuse surviving DIO bounce pages on EC recovery&lt;br/&gt;
Project: fs/lustre-release&lt;br/&gt;
Branch: master&lt;br/&gt;
Current Patch Set: 1&lt;br/&gt;
Commit: 7f002b6ce795f7a7c1bfc750c9386c723072106c&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="499934" author="JIRAUSER22400" created="Thu, 20 Aug 2026 01:17:11 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;For the above patch #67878 (not ready to be reviewed yet): Preserve successfully filled unaligned DIO bounce pages across the CIT_EC_RD restart and adopt them as EC_DPG_UPTODATE so healthy stripes are not re-fetched.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=adilger&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;adilger&quot;&gt;adilger&lt;/a&gt; do you think it worth to do? It surely would introduce some complexity, whereas it could avoid the cost of stripe data refetches in the CIT_EC_RD round.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="500036" author="adilger" created="Thu, 20 Aug 2026 16:24:24 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;It&apos;s essentially turning DIO into cached IO, which is the opposite of what someone wants if using DIO?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="500079" author="JIRAUSER19404" created="Fri, 21 Aug 2026 00:37:12 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I&apos;m incline to store the raw data in OBD_POOL and do not release those pages at the end of the CIT_RD round, then reuse them in the CIT_EC_RD round.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It&apos;s indeed cached I/O, but cached in our own pool, not the page cache. To get rid of the complexity of Page cache. Is that make sense? Or we just retrieve all pages again in the CIT_EC_RD round?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
